00:33:29.340 --> 00:33:29.980
Then where is...

00:33:30.320 --> 00:33:31.260
Chief, this'll kill you.

00:33:31.320 --> 00:33:31.660
I bet.

00:33:31.820 --> 00:33:32.620
Right in that cab.

00:33:32.780 --> 00:33:34.040
Blackie, the runt, and the baby.

00:33:34.140 --> 00:33:34.980
The whole caboodle of them.

00:33:35.660 --> 00:33:37.580
All I gotta say is they better be in there.

00:33:37.720 --> 00:33:38.160
They are.

00:33:38.300 --> 00:33:39.120
And will they be surprised?

00:33:44.620 --> 00:33:46.350
All right, come on out, wise guys.

00:33:49.040 --> 00:33:50.520
You mallet head.

00:33:51.030 --> 00:33:51.970
Now, Chief, take it easy.

00:33:52.310 --> 00:33:54.810
I don't know what keeps me from where you are.

00:34:00.920 --> 00:34:14.020
Wait a minute, driver. Good evening. I'm from the Child Welfare Bureau.

00:34:14.710 --> 00:34:17.510
I'm looking for Mrs. Peyton, Mrs. Geraldine Peyton.

00:34:17.630 --> 00:34:20.390
Well, it's about time somebody made her take care of that baby.

00:34:20.930 --> 00:34:23.250
If I were you, I'd make her take it back to her sisters.

00:34:23.740 --> 00:34:24.360
Her sisters?

00:34:24.790 --> 00:34:27.590
Yes. That's where she says she kept it all the time.

00:34:27.980 --> 00:34:29.960
Oh, I see. Well, how long has she had the...

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:36.090
baby here? Just a couple of days. Well, your evidence is very important. Have you any idea

00:34:36.090 --> 00:34:40.230
where I could find Mrs. Payton at the moment? She went out several hours ago to visit a friend,

00:34:40.630 --> 00:34:45.820
a Mr. Boston Blackie on Park Avenue. And I'll bet a cookie he's no good either. I'll bet you a

00:34:45.820 --> 00:34:51.020
cake you're right. So she left a message where she was going, huh? Yes, because she was expecting

00:34:51.020 --> 00:34:59.000
someone else to call. Oh, I see. Her husband. Did he show up? Right after she left. Are you sure he

00:34:59.000 --> 00:34:59.520
He was her husband.

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:00.880
He said he was.

00:35:01.470 --> 00:35:02.850
Anyway, I gave him the address.

00:35:03.460 --> 00:35:04.380
Why, is there something wrong?

00:35:05.530 --> 00:35:06.710
No, no, everything's fine.

00:35:10.900 --> 00:35:11.740
Thank you very much.

00:35:24.890 --> 00:35:26.030
And we're gonna take the kid inside?

00:35:26.270 --> 00:35:27.690
No, we're gonna hold on to it a while longer.

00:35:28.760 --> 00:35:29.980
Say, runt, if Jerry was...

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:34.520
running away from somebody why would she leave a message where she went how should I know did

00:35:35.150 --> 00:35:42.490
she yeah I understand your feelings Mrs. Fainton but we have a murder to solve and I must ask you

00:35:42.490 --> 00:35:47.510
a few questions that's why I've sent for you I'll tell you everything I know but what about my baby

00:35:47.510 --> 00:35:51.760
we're doing everything possible why did you leave your baby at Blackie's apartment because I thought

00:35:51.760 --> 00:35:55.920
he'd be safe there just what was your relationship with Blackie while your husband was in prison well

00:35:56.970 --> 00:35:59.220
we were seeing each other how often

00:36:00.030 --> 00:36:05.370
twice a week. I was alone. Your husband's parole came as a surprise to you, didn't it? Yes. You see,

00:36:05.430 --> 00:36:11.140
he never said anything to me about it. How could he? The records show you never wrote him or visited

00:36:11.140 --> 00:36:19.460
him in prison. I know. I was so busy making a living for myself and the baby. Are you trying

00:36:19.460 --> 00:36:27.630
to say that I helped Blackie kill him? Then he did kill your husband. Now maybe you'll tell me

00:36:27.630 --> 00:36:28.830
exactly how it did happen.

00:36:30.060 --> 00:36:32.820
Well, I was waiting for Blackie to come home.

00:36:33.570 --> 00:36:35.590
He was only there a short time when John showed up.

00:36:36.310 --> 00:36:37.950
He accused us of double-crossing him.

00:36:38.380 --> 00:36:39.400
What did Blackie say to that?

00:36:40.140 --> 00:36:40.860
Well, they quarreled.

00:36:41.440 --> 00:36:42.480
And then they started to fight.

00:36:43.050 --> 00:36:45.490
Blackie pulled out a gun, and before I knew it, they were wrestling for it.

00:36:45.630 --> 00:36:47.380
I was a shot, and...

00:36:48.180 --> 00:36:48.760
And then what happened?

00:36:49.420 --> 00:36:51.780
I know, and someone took me out of the apartment and called a cab.

00:36:52.800 --> 00:36:53.120
Mm-hmm.

00:36:54.710 --> 00:36:55.110
Mm-hmm.

00:37:00.160 --> 00:37:03.860
I called Blackie's apartment all night and this morning, but there was no answer.

00:37:04.860 --> 00:37:06.500
Why would Blackie want to hold on to your baby?

00:37:06.660 --> 00:37:09.150
I don't know, but I'm sure he's up to something.

00:37:09.800 --> 00:37:12.040
In that case, there's another interested party I think you should meet.

00:37:12.790 --> 00:37:13.830
Send Mr. Harcourt in.

00:37:14.700 --> 00:37:16.290
Mr. Harcourt? Who's he?

00:37:20.890 --> 00:37:23.430
Mr. Harcourt? This is Mrs. Payton.

00:37:26.980 --> 00:37:29.980
I'm the attorney representing Mr. Cyrus Payton, your lead husband's father.

00:37:31.210 --> 00:37:31.810
What does he want?

00:37:32.030 --> 00:37:34.390
Well, I'm sure that you, as a parent, can appreciate his feelings.

00:37:35.280 --> 00:37:38.420
Mr. Payton received word this morning from an anonymous source

00:37:38.420 --> 00:37:42.150
that he has a grandchild by Mrs. Payton and his unfortunate son.

00:37:42.870 --> 00:37:43.950
You mean he didn't know that?

00:37:44.370 --> 00:37:45.130
Strangely enough, no.

00:37:45.660 --> 00:37:46.400
So is his attorney.

00:37:46.600 --> 00:37:48.500
It's my duty to see that he is not victimized.

00:37:48.700 --> 00:37:49.640
Tell him he needn't worry.

00:37:50.060 --> 00:37:53.200
Old man Payton has no claim on my son, and I don't want anything from him.

00:37:53.360 --> 00:37:54.260
Just a minute, Mrs. Payton.

00:37:55.060 --> 00:37:56.280
No use getting yourself upset.

00:37:57.090 --> 00:37:59.510
Before any action can be taken, we're going to have to find your baby.

00:38:00.120 --> 00:38:01.460
I'm afraid I don't quite understand.

00:38:01.620 --> 00:38:02.400
The baby is missing.

00:38:02.520 --> 00:38:03.640
Missing? Do you mean kidnapped?

00:38:04.030 --> 00:38:07.000
Well, shall we say temporarily misplaced.

00:38:08.640 --> 00:38:09.680
Say, Chief, you know, I...

00:38:10.020 --> 00:38:12.000
Oh, excuse me.

00:38:12.220 --> 00:38:13.140
Well, you're in. What is it?

00:38:13.790 --> 00:38:16.170
Well, Chief, remember last night I got the number off of the cab

00:38:16.170 --> 00:38:17.430
that Blackie and the runner steeped in.

00:38:17.550 --> 00:38:19.270
If you hadn't, you'd be pounding a beat today.

00:38:19.550 --> 00:38:20.710
Yeah, and you know what I did?

00:38:20.830 --> 00:38:22.590
I found out where they were dropped off, I hope.

00:38:23.060 --> 00:38:24.760
That's right, but you'll never guess where.

00:38:24.920 --> 00:38:25.680
At Blackie's apartment.

00:38:26.880 --> 00:38:27.320
That's right.

00:38:27.700 --> 00:38:29.760
Come on, I'll have your baby back for you in half an hour.

00:38:31.600 --> 00:38:40.700
How does he do it? I'm going to read a book sometime and get as smart as he is.

00:38:41.920 --> 00:38:50.850
Go to sleep, my baby, and close the ears.

00:38:51.360 --> 00:38:58.350
Go to sleep, my baby, and close the ears.

00:39:05.050 --> 00:39:06.110
Oh, what's the use?

00:39:06.550 --> 00:39:08.670
Hey, maybe we ought to sing some grand opera.

00:39:08.940 --> 00:39:09.980
They always put me to sleep.

00:39:10.950 --> 00:39:11.830
This is silly.

00:39:11.930 --> 00:39:14.570
Why didn't you leave the baby at Jerry's when you were there the last time?

00:39:14.650 --> 00:39:15.910
Well, the whole thing sounds fishy, Mamie.

00:39:16.330 --> 00:39:19.070
Jerry told a landlady that she was keeping the kid at his sister's home.

00:39:19.550 --> 00:39:20.670
Well, what's wrong with that?

00:39:21.610 --> 00:39:23.150
I happen to know she hasn't got a sister.

00:39:24.060 --> 00:39:24.360
What?

00:39:25.560 --> 00:39:27.980
I'm afraid our sweet little Jerry is trying to pull a fast one.

00:39:28.940 --> 00:39:29.960
Oh, she wouldn't do that to you.

00:39:30.360 --> 00:39:32.550
Well, then why didn't she come out and tell the truth about the murder?

00:39:32.880 --> 00:39:33.340
I don't know.

00:39:34.330 --> 00:39:35.230
Well, there's only one thing to do.

00:39:35.370 --> 00:39:37.150
Well, maybe you'll have to take the baby over to Jerry's apartment.

00:39:37.660 --> 00:39:39.880
Now you're talking. Hey!

00:39:40.970 --> 00:39:42.950
The address is 1706 East Drive.

00:39:43.110 --> 00:39:44.950
Now, tell her you found it at the railroad station. Tell her anything.

00:39:45.300 --> 00:39:46.540
Wait a minute. Isn't it enough?

00:39:46.580 --> 00:39:49.280
You got me mixed up in a murder, now you want me arrested as a kidnapper.

00:39:49.380 --> 00:39:51.080
Well, if you're arrested, Mamie, we'll come and visit you,

00:39:51.080 --> 00:39:52.380
and we'll send you flowers and candy.

00:39:52.480 --> 00:39:55.400
Never mind the flowers. If I get pinched, you'll need them yourself.

00:39:56.180 --> 00:39:58.260
Hey, Mamie, ain't that cute?

00:40:00.990 --> 00:40:02.430
And doesn't that give you some ideas?

00:40:02.850 --> 00:40:03.850
Yes, it does.

00:40:04.330 --> 00:40:06.950
That you're a crazy galoot, and I'm not going to get you out of any more jams.

00:40:07.070 --> 00:40:08.350
Does that give you any ideas?

00:40:08.510 --> 00:40:09.970
Yeah. Out the back way. Hurry.

00:40:10.190 --> 00:40:11.250
You're not kidding, brother.

00:40:17.350 --> 00:40:17.890
Who's there?

00:40:18.420 --> 00:40:19.320
It's me, Jerry.

00:40:19.850 --> 00:40:21.430
Don't you think that we are? Keep out of sight.

00:40:26.630 --> 00:40:29.390
Come in. Come in. I hope the room is large enough.

00:40:34.410 --> 00:40:36.310
All right, Blackie, let's make it short and sweet.

00:40:36.680 --> 00:40:38.000
Quite a convoy you brought with you.

00:40:38.280 --> 00:40:40.180
I'm sorry, Blackie, but I've come for my baby.

00:40:40.400 --> 00:40:40.840
Where is he?

00:40:41.830 --> 00:40:42.750
Come on, cut out the stalling.

00:40:42.770 --> 00:40:43.510
We know the whole story.

00:40:43.770 --> 00:40:44.670
Take a look around, Matthews.

00:40:44.770 --> 00:40:50.560
You miss your baby very much, Jerry?

00:40:51.190 --> 00:40:51.950
What do you mean by that?

00:40:52.760 --> 00:40:53.560
Kid ain't here, Chief.

00:40:53.820 --> 00:40:55.040
He isn't here.

00:40:55.890 --> 00:40:56.730
What have you done with him?

00:40:57.090 --> 00:40:58.330
You're flirting with dynamite, Blackie.

00:41:00.490 --> 00:41:00.850
Hello?

00:41:02.800 --> 00:41:03.540
Hello, Archie?

00:41:04.060 --> 00:41:04.720
Hello, Runt.

00:41:05.120 --> 00:41:06.020
Don't worry about a plane.

00:41:06.700 --> 00:41:09.380
Yeah, you know who took you know what to you know where.

00:41:10.200 --> 00:41:13.500
Listen, Runt, you can tell you know who that I know what's what, and I'll soon find out where.

00:41:14.820 --> 00:41:29.500
I think the janitors got nothing else to do but looking after their pooches.

00:41:39.660 --> 00:41:41.460
Blackie, what kind of a stunt are you trying to pull with this baby?

00:41:41.640 --> 00:41:42.460
I can't tell you yet.

00:41:42.640 --> 00:41:43.340
I think you'd better.

00:41:44.120 --> 00:41:46.680
I guess you know Mrs. Payton has already implicated you in the murder of her husband.

00:41:46.900 --> 00:41:48.240
I beg your pardon.

00:41:48.490 --> 00:41:49.050
What did you say?

00:41:49.150 --> 00:41:49.870
You heard what I said.

00:41:50.400 --> 00:41:51.620
I couldn't help it, Blackie.

00:41:51.740 --> 00:41:52.660
I had to tell the truth.

00:41:52.820 --> 00:41:53.320
The truth, huh?

00:41:53.520 --> 00:41:54.860
Just what did you tell the inspector?

00:41:55.760 --> 00:41:56.480
You'd better answer me.

00:41:56.660 --> 00:41:58.940
Young man, you don't realize the seriousness of this.

00:41:59.380 --> 00:41:59.960
If there's any...

00:42:00.220 --> 00:42:01.940
Mr. Payton's prepared to take drastic action.

00:42:02.040 --> 00:42:03.220
And may I ask who you are, sir?

00:42:03.380 --> 00:42:04.320
My name's Harcourt.

00:42:04.700 --> 00:42:06.000
I'm attorney for Mr. Payton Senior.

00:42:06.440 --> 00:42:06.700
Oh.

00:42:07.580 --> 00:42:10.040
Well, Jerry told me old man Payton didn't know there was a baby.

00:42:10.160 --> 00:42:11.360
How did he find out so suddenly?

00:42:11.860 --> 00:42:13.060
He received this note today.

00:42:13.340 --> 00:42:19.580
I wonder if you know your grandson is being badly neglected by Mrs. Geraldine Payton.

00:42:19.760 --> 00:42:20.360
That's a lie.

00:42:20.630 --> 00:42:21.850
I take very good care of him.

00:42:22.250 --> 00:42:23.270
Go on, Mr. Harcourt.

00:42:23.470 --> 00:42:24.770
Something should be done about it.

00:42:25.210 --> 00:42:25.870
Can I see that, please?

00:42:26.330 --> 00:42:28.050
I'm not privileged to let it out of my possession.

00:42:28.350 --> 00:42:29.090
Well, who wrote the note?

00:42:29.310 --> 00:42:29.970
It's merely signed...

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:34.960
a friend a friend whoever wrote that note's even afraid to sign a name doesn't it strike you as

00:42:34.960 --> 00:42:39.060
strange inspected that the baby receives all this publicity the same day young peyton was murdered

00:42:39.060 --> 00:42:43.100
you can bet it's strange that's why you're going down to headquarters come on i'll take your hands

00:43:00.160 --> 00:43:01.240
Look at them, don't they play cute.

00:43:01.540 --> 00:43:02.920
You, you, Blackie, come here!

00:43:03.620 --> 00:43:06.320
Hell, you stupid ox!

00:43:08.840 --> 00:43:11.620
I'd better phone the Humane Society and tell them what's going on here.

00:43:13.840 --> 00:43:14.880
Get them away somehow.

00:43:15.980 --> 00:43:16.800
Call their backpack.

00:43:18.880 --> 00:43:20.680
Don't worry, Mr. Hart, hold on, here we go.

00:43:21.980 --> 00:43:23.340
Take it easy, Faraday.

00:43:25.600 --> 00:43:26.700
I'll meet you at the dawn time.

00:43:28.020 --> 00:43:29.780
Blackie! Come back here!

00:43:33.360 --> 00:43:49.770
You scared me.

00:43:49.810 --> 00:43:50.670
I scared you.

00:43:50.790 --> 00:43:52.110
What are you doing climbing in windows?

00:43:52.430 --> 00:43:53.950
Oh, Mamie, this ain't just any old window.

00:43:54.210 --> 00:43:54.710
That's just what I mean.

00:43:54.770 --> 00:43:56.580
Yesterday I was happy leading a quiet life.

00:43:56.700 --> 00:43:58.570
Now look at me shaking like a bowl of jelly.

00:43:58.830 --> 00:43:59.570
Oh, but honey, I...

00:43:59.570 --> 00:43:59.970
Don't you...

00:44:01.600 --> 00:44:02.570
I've given the baby back.

00:44:04.490 --> 00:44:06.250
Hey, Blackie and Mike, glad to see you.

00:44:06.390 --> 00:44:06.770
Mamie here.

00:44:06.790 --> 00:44:08.570
Mamie says shut up and Mamie says beat it.

00:44:08.770 --> 00:44:10.010
Oh, a lover's quarrel, huh?

00:44:10.290 --> 00:44:11.150
And in the dark, too.

00:44:12.660 --> 00:44:14.180
Well, you'll have to do that in your spare time.

00:44:14.300 --> 00:44:15.660
I've got more important matters to take up.

00:44:15.760 --> 00:44:16.960
And I got to tell you.

00:44:17.080 --> 00:44:18.640
I just checked with the Bureau of Vital Statistics.

00:44:18.840 --> 00:44:19.120
You did?

00:44:19.240 --> 00:44:21.720
There's no birth record of a child named Peyton in the last three years.

00:44:22.170 --> 00:44:23.150
Then that kid is a ringer.

00:44:23.270 --> 00:44:23.430
Right.

00:44:23.590 --> 00:44:26.250
And for that, I had to break my neck and nearly got arrested as a kidnapper.

00:44:26.310 --> 00:44:26.910
It was all an act.

00:44:27.280 --> 00:44:29.900
Jerry's working with somebody and they're trying to pull a fast shake down on old man.

00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:34.270
Payton. Now, they needed some fall guys to take care of young Payton, so we were elected to take

00:44:34.270 --> 00:44:38.590
the rap. Well, why don't we go to Faraday and spill the works? Do you think he's going to believe us?

00:44:38.630 --> 00:44:42.450
No, we've got to clear ourselves, Mamie, or go to jail. Well, nobody's going to put me in the pokey.

00:44:42.550 --> 00:44:48.870
I'm going to Faraday and talk my head off. I don't blame you, Mamie. I understand

00:44:48.870 --> 00:44:54.830
exactly how you feel. Of course, I was hoping you'd help us out, but I wouldn't want to come

00:44:54.830 --> 00:44:58.830
between you and Mamie, Rudd. You're too good a pal. Well, Mackie.

00:45:00.090 --> 00:45:01.250
I never let you down before.

00:45:01.490 --> 00:45:04.090
Oh, skip it. I'll handle it somehow. Alone.

00:45:04.490 --> 00:45:06.450
No, but you're the best friend I ever had.

00:45:06.880 --> 00:45:09.280
We pulled through some mighty tough jams together, haven't we, Rod?

00:45:09.810 --> 00:45:10.610
Yes, we did.

00:45:10.790 --> 00:45:12.470
Yes, we did. But don't worry.

00:45:16.020 --> 00:45:17.480
I'll handle this alone somehow.

00:45:20.260 --> 00:45:21.340
I'll take the rap myself.

00:45:22.520 --> 00:45:23.680
I'm not gonna desert you, Blackie.

00:45:23.980 --> 00:45:26.880
I'm gonna stick. I'm gonna stick like I've never stuck before.

00:45:27.080 --> 00:45:27.440
No.

00:45:27.860 --> 00:45:28.300
Yes.

00:45:28.500 --> 00:45:28.840
No.

00:45:29.260 --> 00:45:29.680
Yes.

00:45:30.570 --> 00:45:33.390
Will you two stop this before I start born?

00:45:34.520 --> 00:45:35.840
Oh, Mamie, you're terrific.

00:45:36.120 --> 00:45:37.220
I knew you wouldn't let us down.

00:45:37.320 --> 00:45:38.180
Wait a minute, I didn't say...

00:45:38.180 --> 00:45:39.020
Have you ever been a secretary?

00:45:39.580 --> 00:45:39.900
Why?

00:45:40.140 --> 00:45:41.180
Do you want me to sit on your lap?

00:45:41.660 --> 00:45:42.300
Maybe later.

00:45:42.420 --> 00:45:44.580
Right now, I want you to phone Jerry and say you're Peyton's secretary.

00:45:44.800 --> 00:45:45.380
Peyton's secretary?

00:45:45.600 --> 00:45:45.700
That's right.

00:45:45.880 --> 00:45:46.540
I won't do it.

00:45:46.600 --> 00:45:47.260
That's forgery.

00:45:47.580 --> 00:45:47.920
Oh, Mamie.

00:45:48.060 --> 00:45:51.420
Oh, now, look, Blackie, we've got 150 years in jail waiting for us

00:45:51.420 --> 00:45:52.600
and the chair at the end of that.

00:45:52.660 --> 00:45:53.680
Then what have we got to lose?

00:45:53.880 --> 00:45:55.140
I'll dial the number for you.

00:45:55.950 --> 00:45:56.890
Now, when you get Jerry,

00:45:57.610 --> 00:45:59.970
you say that Cyrus W. Peyton wants to speak.

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:22.330
is that clear here we go again yes this is mrs payton my father-in-law yes mr payton

00:46:22.330 --> 00:46:28.090
i just arrived in town and heard about the baby

00:46:30.280 --> 00:46:39.220
you got it back fine fine well just a moment young lady there's no need of losing your temper

00:46:39.880 --> 00:46:48.000
after all i'm the one who really should be angry you know well very well i'll be brief i think we

00:46:48.000 --> 00:46:57.860
should have a little talk and possibly reach some sort of settlement yes good i'll be there within

00:46:57.860 --> 00:46:59.580
the hour goodbye

00:47:02.430 --> 00:47:03.930
Yes, sir, the whole idea is very clear.

00:47:04.580 --> 00:47:07.840
This is a shakedown for Big Doe, and Blackie's in it with that Jerry girl.

00:47:08.180 --> 00:47:09.500
I think we got something there, Chief.

